>exact command</b> (using backslashes <code data-path-to-node="4" data-index-in-node="42">\</code>):</p><pre><code class="language-powershell" data-path-to-node="5">vol <span class="hljs-operator">-f</span> <span class="hljs-string">"dumps\THUNDERJACK_20260102_204204.dmp"</span> windows.info
</code></pre><h3 data-path-to-node="6"><b data-path-to-node="6" data-index-in-node="0">Step 2: Read the Output</b></h3><p data-path-to-node="7">Volatility will verify the file header and scan the Kernel Debugger Block (KDBG). Look for these two lines:</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="8"><li><p data-path-to-node="8,0,0"><b data-path-to-node="8,0,0" data-index-in-node="0"><code data-path-to-node="8,0,0" data-index-in-node="0">DtB</code></b> (or <code data-path-to-node="8,0,0" data-index-in-node="8">DirectoryTableBase</code>): This is the <b data-path-to-node="8,0,0" data-index-in-node="41">Master Key</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="8,1,0"><b data-path-to-node="8,1,0" data-index-in-node="0"><code data-path-to-node=